      "head_commit": {
        "id": "b1d67a5c4de7254ceb162aca5bab2aacc1c9354a",
        "tree_id": "864b7db768847fe75eb9874653b2781c7532c1e8",
        "message": "feat(PR-N4): rewind and server-side shot validation\n\nA 31-frame tick->world ring rewinds to the shooter's tick. A tick outside\nthe ring is stale-shot, never approximated with the newest state. Validation\norder: identity, cooldown, squared range, integer LOS.\n\nRange is bigint squared distance in mm^2 — no Math.sqrt, no trigonometry,\nno float (D147). LOS is an integer Bresenham walk over 1000 mm cells with\nendpoints exempt. The client's claimed flag is ignored; only the server's\nNET-006 HitLedger fires a hit (I1/I3).\n\nLocal fuzz: 30 shots -> 4 hits, 16 cooldown refusals, 5 LOS blocks, 4\nout-of-range, 1 stale tick; deterministic verdict sequence. Not RTT, not a\nloss matrix, not a soak. Range/cooldown are tunables until PR-S1.\n\nGDD-NETCODE 0.7 (I9): lag-comp rule, four sourced/tunable numbers, verdict\ncontract. PR-N4 acc repaired to a real vitest command (tenth broken form).\nB2 caught the append-only prototype report's ownership: qa-engineer added\nas co-owner, as for PR-N3.\n\nAcceptance: lagcomp 10/10, full 142/142, verify 17/17, tracer green.\n\nAgent: netcode-engineer\nTask: PR-N4",
